T.append(L(P+"t09","CRUD Operations (Servlets)","high",
"CRUD operations in servlets use Create, Read, Update and Delete actions mapped to SQL INSERT, SELECT, UPDATE and DELETE through JDBC, usually via a DAO class.",
"CRUD matlab Create, Read, Update, Delete. Servlet form data leta hai, JDBC PreparedStatement se database me INSERT/SELECT/UPDATE/DELETE karta hai aur result dikhata hai.",
"A library desk: add a book (create), look up (read), correct details (update) and remove old books (delete).",
"StudentServlet with action parameter: add → INSERT; list → SELECT; update → UPDATE; delete → DELETE using PreparedStatement.",
["Create: INSERT; Read: SELECT; Update: UPDATE; Delete: DELETE.","Use doPost for create/update/delete and doGet for read.","DAO pattern separates database code from servlet.","Use PreparedStatement to avoid SQL injection.","Redirect after POST to avoid duplicate submission.","Close resources with try-with-resources."],
["Four operations and SQL.","DAO.","Redirect after POST."],
["Write CRUD with servlet+JDBC.","Explain DAO.","Avoid injection."],
["Building SQL with string concatenation.","Not handling SQLException."],
[E("explain with example","Write servlet code for inserting a student.","PreparedStatement INSERT in doPost."),
 E("viva","Why redirect after POST?","To prevent form resubmission on refresh (PRG pattern).")],
[Q("MCQ","SQL for Read:","SELECT","",["INSERT","SELECT","UPDATE","DELETE"]),
 Q("true/false","DAO separates DB code from servlet.","True",""),
 Q("short answer","Method that returns row count?","executeUpdate()",""),
 Q("scenario","Delete student with id from request. Safe approach?","PreparedStatement with ? parameter",""),
 Q("comparison","doGet vs doPost for create.","doPost is preferred for changes; doGet for reads.","")],
"CRUD in servlets: INSERT/SELECT/UPDATE/DELETE via JDBC PreparedStatement; DAO; PRG redirect.",
syntax="PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement(\"INSERT INTO student(id,name) VALUES(?,?)\");",
code="@WebServlet(\"/student\")\npublic class StudentServlet extends HttpServlet {\n  protected void doPost(HttpServletRequest rq, HttpServletResponse rs) throws IOException {\n    String act = rq.getParameter(\"action\");\n    try (Connection c = DriverManager.getConnection(\"jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/college\",\"root\",\"root\")) {\n      if (\"add\".equals(act)) {\n        PreparedStatement p = c.prepareStatement(\"INSERT INTO student(id,name) VALUES(?,?)\");\n        p.setInt(1, Integer.parseInt(rq.getParameter(\"id\"))); p.setString(2, rq.getParameter(\"name\")); p.executeUpdate();\n      } else if (\"delete\".equals(act)) {\n        PreparedStatement p = c.prepareStatement(\"DELETE FROM student WHERE id=?\");\n        p.setInt(1, Integer.parseInt(rq.getParameter(\"id\"))); p.executeUpdate();\n      }\n    } catch (SQLException e) { throw new IOException(e); }\n    rs.sendRedirect(\"student\");\n  }\n}",
expectedOutput="Form add id=3,name=Meena → row inserted → redirect to list",
codeExplanation="The action parameter selects the operation; PreparedStatement binds values; redirect avoids duplicate submits.",
apis=["PreparedStatement","executeUpdate","executeQuery","HttpServletResponse.sendRedirect"],
commonErrors=["NumberFormatException for non-numeric id.","SQLIntegrityConstraintViolation for duplicate id."]))
